1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,333
A failed transaction shouldn't need a support ticket.

2
00:00:03,333 --> 00:00:09,333
GasBack offers a fixed sponsor rebate,
paid only after the failure is independently verified.

3
00:00:12,375 --> 00:00:14,208
Before the user acts.

4
00:00:14,208 --> 00:00:18,125
The sponsor approves this exact transaction intent.

5
00:00:18,125 --> 00:00:22,750
The ticket fixes the recipient the amount and the claim window.

6
00:00:22,750 --> 00:00:25,000
It's a fixed subsidy,

7
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:26,875
not a full gas refund.

8
00:00:28,625 --> 00:00:31,458
This is our real Sepolia transaction.

9
00:00:31,708 --> 00:00:36,292
We deliberately make it revert so the failure is reproducible.

10
00:00:36,292 --> 00:00:39,167
The proof establishes what happened.

11
00:00:39,167 --> 00:00:41,875
It doesn't decide who was at fault.

12
00:00:42,708 --> 00:00:46,333
Once attestation is ready, the relayer gets a proof

13
00:00:46,542 --> 00:00:50,542
Creditcoin checks it through the native Attestcoin verifier.

14
00:00:50,542 --> 00:00:54,917
The vault reads those verified
bytes and checks the sponsor's policy.

15
00:00:54,917 --> 00:00:57,625
The actual preparation time is shown here.

16
00:01:01,667 --> 00:01:05,208
The matching failure receives one test CTC.

17
00:01:05,417 --> 00:01:07,583
Here's the mined claim receipt.

18
00:01:07,583 --> 00:01:12,792
A relayer can submit the proof, but
can't change who gets paid or how much.

19
00:01:16,750 --> 00:01:21,125
Try the same claim again and the read only check rejects it.

20
00:01:21,833 --> 00:01:27,167
Local tests also reject an altered
payload and a successful source receipt.

21
00:01:27,917 --> 00:01:30,542
These checks aren't additional payments.

22
00:01:31,458 --> 00:01:36,875
GasBack turns a failed receipt on another
chain into a bounded sponsorship decision.

23
00:01:37,417 --> 00:01:42,208
You can inspect the source code, proof policy and payment yourself.

24
00:01:42,792 --> 00:01:45,792
Everything shown uses test assets.
